claim:
\subsection{Composition and within-group weighting}\label{sec:appendix-mixture}
On supported $A_\ell$, keep electricity-qualified $R$ and its complement $U=A\setminus R$ fixed, and write $Y=|B_{30}|$. Index station weighting by 0 and the target activity perspective by 1. For group $g\in\{U,R\}$, let $\pi_g^a$ be its weight share and $F_g^b$ its conditional distribution under weighting perspective $b$. The four hybrid distributions and their common-rule medians are
\begin{equation}
F_{ab}(y)=\sum_{g\in\{U,R\}}\pi_g^aF_g^b(y),
\qquad m_{ab}=Q_{F_{ab}}(0.5),\quad a,b\in\{0,1\}.
\label{eq:extension-mixture}
\end{equation}
Here $a$ selects group shares and $b$ selects within-group weights. Averaging the two replacement orders gives
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\Delta_{\mathrm{comp}}&=\tfrac12[(m_{10}-m_{00})+(m_{11}-m_{01})],\\
\Delta_{\mathrm{within}}&=\tfrac12[(m_{01}-m_{00})+(m_{11}-m_{10})],\\
\Delta_{\mathrm{comp}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{within}}&=m_{11}-m_{00}.
\end{aligned}
\label{eq:symmetric-mixture}
\end{equation}
This accounting separates composition from within-group distribution changes \citep{FortinLemieuxFirpo2011,DiNardoFortinLemieux1996}. Table~\ref{tab:measurement-mixture} uses 2,000 shared-station resamples conditional on observed prices, support and membership. Components add at the point estimate and in each draw. Marginal percentile endpoints are reported separately.

reported_value:
\subsection{Composition and within-group weighting}\label{sec:appendix-mixture}
On supported $A_\ell$, keep electricity-qualified $R$ and its complement $U=A\setminus R$ fixed, and write $Y=|B_{30}|$. Index station weighting by 0 and the target activity perspective by 1. For group $g\in\{U,R\}$, let $\pi_g^a$ be its weight share and $F_g^b$ its conditional distribution under weighting perspective $b$. The four hybrid distributions and their common-rule medians are
\begin{equation}
F_{ab}(y)=\sum_{g\in\{U,R\}}\pi_g^aF_g^b(y),
\qquad m_{ab}=Q_{F_{ab}}(0.5),\quad a,b\in\{0,1\}.
\label{eq:extension-mixture}
\end{equation}
Here $a$ selects group shares and $b$ selects within-group weights. Averaging the two replacement orders gives
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\Delta_{\mathrm{comp}}&=\tfrac12[(m_{10}-m_{00})+(m_{11}-m_{01})],\\
\Delta_{\mathrm{within}}&=\tfrac12[(m_{01}-m_{00})+(m_{11}-m_{10})],\\
\Delta_{\mathrm{comp}}+\Delta_{\mathrm{within}}&=m_{11}-m_{00}.
\end{aligned}
\label{eq:symmetric-mixture}
\end{equation}
This accounting separates composition from within-group distribution changes \citep{FortinLemieuxFirpo2011,DiNardoFortinLemieux1996}. Table~\ref{tab:measurement-mixture} uses 2,000 shared-station resamples conditional on observed prices, support and membership. Components add at the point estimate and in each draw. Marginal percentile endpoints are reported separately.
